# Architecture

## Overview

{{ project_name }} is a TypeScript service using Hono with a Bun runtime.

## Project Structure

```
src/
  index.ts               # Bun server entry point
  app.ts                 # Hono app factory
  config.ts              # zod-based env/config validation
  logging.ts             # pino setup
  telemetry.ts           # OpenTelemetry setup
  routers/               # HTTP endpoint definitions
    health.ts            # /healthz, /readyz
  controllers/           # Request orchestration
  services/              # Business logic
  dtos/                  # Zod request/response schemas
{%- if include_clients %}
  clients/               # External API/service clients
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
  db.ts                  # Prisma client setup
  repositories/          # Data access layer
{%- endif %}
tests/
  unit/                  # Fast, isolated unit tests
  integration/           # Tests with real dependencies
  e2e/                   # End-to-end tests
```

## Layering

```
routers (HTTP endpoints, validate with zod)
  -> controllers (orchestrate across services)
    -> services (business logic, framework-agnostic)
{%- if include_clients %}
      -> clients (external API calls)
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
      -> repositories (data access via Prisma)
{%- endif %}
```

DTOs (zod schemas) are used at the router and controller level for API I/O. They are always separate from database models.

## Toolchain

| Tool | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| Bun | Runtime and package manager |
| TypeScript | Type system |
| Biome | Formatting and linting |
| bun test | Testing |
| Hono | HTTP framework |
| OpenTelemetry | Distributed tracing |
| pino | Structured logging |
| zod | Config/env validation and DTOs |
{%- if include_database %}
| Prisma | ORM and database access |
{%- endif %}

## Conventions

- All configuration is in `package.json` and `tsconfig.json`.
- Health endpoints are always available at `/healthz` and `/readyz`.
